From 16f6202be1ab9d0be752aabcba1fd1b80496ff49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chiffathefox <chiffathefoxx@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 21:15:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/46] dirty: pmu: exynos9820 support

Based on the downstream kernel, exynos9820 requires the CPU that's about to go up/down to change the INFORM, GRP1 and GRP2 registers. Trying to change these registers from other CPUs doesn't seem to work. The CPUs going up/down simply hang up. This is the reason for the new cpuhp states as well as a slight rework of the mainline PMU driver.

(cherry picked from commit dfa4dd1cafee8c690e91f38153b6a920547b91e4)
---
 drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile         |   3 +-
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.c     |  80 ++++++++++++----
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos-pmu.h     |   3 +
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos9820-pmu.c | 132 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/cpuhotplug.h           |   2 +
 5 files changed, 202 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos9820-pmu.c

